<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hallucination Mitigation</span>.
Our approach achieves hallucination reductions up to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="33\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>33</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">33\%</annotation></semantics></math> at sentence-level (<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="hal" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">hal</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\%</annotation></semantics></math> at instance-level (<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cha</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), demonstrating its effectiveness in mitigating overall hallucinations.
It also effectively addresses co-occurrence hallucinations, achieving up to a <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="57\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>57</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">57\%</annotation></semantics></math> reduction for <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cog" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cog</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We detail the text-visual and co-occurrence bias analysis in Sec. <a href="#S5" title="5 Ablation Study ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
Furthermore, an accuracy increase of up to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="92\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>92</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">92\%</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> underscores our model’s effectiveness in reducing hallucinations by staying closely aligned with the input image. This improvement highlights our method’s capacity to jointly mitigate multiple types of hallucinations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Information Preservation</span>.
Our method also enhances information preservation, with recall (<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cov" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cov</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> in Tab. <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) dropping by an average of only <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1\%</annotation></semantics></math>, compared to an average drop of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.2\%</annotation></semantics></math> in other methods, and even increasing by <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> when using the baseline mPLUG-Owl2 on the AMBER dataset.
Higher recall indicates that our model retrieves a broader range of objects from visual inputs. Additionally, results in Tab. <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.1 Results on Open-ended Generation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> an increase of up to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45\%</annotation></semantics></math> in detailedness (<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Det" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Det</annotation></semantics></math>), further demonstrating our method’s effectiveness in retrieving all relevant visual details and mitigating visual forgetting.</p>
</div>
