<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Other Results of POPE</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report our experimental results on the POPE dataset, in addition to MSCOCO and adversarial settings, in Tab. <a href="#A8.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix H Other Results of POPE ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. The results indicate that our method improves performance across all baseline MLLMs, with more significant gains observed in the adversarial setting.
This discrepancy likely arises because adversarial scenarios require models to rely more heavily on visual inputs, aligning with our method’s focus on enhancing visual influence. Conversely, for popular and random objects, textual data often provides sufficient statistical information, reducing the necessity for increased visual input reliance.</p>
</div>
