<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Different Sampling Strategies</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tab. <a href="#A9.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix I Different Sampling Strategies ‣ Mitigating Multimodal Hallucinations via Gradient-based Self-Reflection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> presents an ablation study on sampling strategies (non-greedy vs. greedy).
We follow the non-greedy sampling setting of VCD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>, where both top-p and temperature are set to 1. As shown, our method consistently improves performance across both sampling strategies.</p>
</div>
